    "interconnection": "The same carrier shades the ascent and supplies its wallbounce. The high mirror sends sunlight through the fixed pair into the King below. Swapping at that mirror leaves an echo holding the lower shutter while bringing the player back to the only lantern. The lantern then shades the return crossing to the newly exposed King; the echo and optical state remain relevant through both native blooms.",
    "solution": "Save an echo at the lower west station, leaving the lantern. Catch the moving shade and reel up underneath its two sunlight crossings. Near its upper turn, pay out and swing right; updash beside its right face and hold Jump for the wallbounce. Brake onto the sheltered upper lip. Cut down-right to turn the mirror; its beam now enters the fixed upper mouth and emerges behind the King. Step onto the broad brass gallery and swap, leaving the echo there to hold the lower shutter. Back west, deliberately pick up the lantern and carry its shade through the two lower sunlight bands. Set it down beyond the second band. Jump over the pod and cut downward with Jump held; climb in its loft, updash, then drift onto the broad boss shelf. Jump in and strike from the unlit side; retreat, then jump the responding glove/wave and strike after his brief recovery. The real second bloom lowers his guard and opens the gate. Rest on the yielded King, then jump and dash over the still-open portal into the exit.",
    "novelty": "Three successive roles for one high address: a moving-wall destination, an optical control and the persistent echo weight for a lower return. The boss receives the same light configured on that return’s opposite end, while the lantern deliberately stayed outside the ascent.",
    "nearestExisting": "F45 supplies an upper address/echo return with cargo, F46 supplies a shared moving shade as a wallbounce face, and F57 supplies moving-anchor departure timing. Here their return releases a native multi-bloom King rather than just an exit.",
